From cca34473de5d3da3f23c019257dc8a667ab81059 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gaia <build@heygaia.io>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 07:18:22 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] fix(net): a navigation a document starts names it, and a post
 carries its Origin

Every navigation went out as if typed into the address bar: Sec-Fetch-Site
none, no Referer, and a form post with no Origin. A login form posted that
way fails CSRF guards that check Origin or Referer (Django refuses an https
post without a Referer), and a link or script navigation looked like a
direct visit.

A navigation the page started (form submission, link, location change,
whether driven through the Page API or the CDP server's live-page loop) now
carries the starting document as initiator: Sec-Fetch-Site from its origin,
a Referer under the default referrer policy, and document.referrer as
before. Requests whose method is neither GET nor HEAD carry Origin as the
Fetch standard has them (null where an https page posts to http), so a
same-origin script POST gets it too. A frame's scripts are fetched as the
frame's script subresources rather than as navigations.

Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Tm2SNEJ42hMPiZ6cFb8Vih
